course: dictionary
lesson: 1008
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Bombardier is one of them. Look at the words next to it: in «The bombardier beetle sprays a boiling hot spray», the word beetle tells you that bombardier is a kind of insect.
explain: In a war story, «The bombardier aimed at the target» means something different. Ask who is doing the action: a person in a bomber aircraft's crew, or an animal? The clues point you to the right meaning. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one still makes sense.
explain: Clue words such as beetle, aircraft, crew or army do the work for you. Once you know which meaning fits, you can understand the sentence, and you can use the word correctly in your own writing.
fact: Bombardier has three meanings: a crew member who aims and releases bombs on a bomber aircraft, a rank in the British Royal Artillery like a corporal, and a type of beetle.
fact: A bombardier beetle sprays a hot, stinging chemical from its back end to defend itself.
fact: «The bombardier beetle mixes two chemicals in a chamber in its tail», and they react to make a burst of heat.
fact: The spray comes out near boiling point, with a pop, in fast pulses, hundreds a second.
fact: A context clue is a word near the unknown word that helps you decide its meaning.
exercise: «The bombardier aimed and released the bombs from the plane.» What is a bombardier here? | A kind of cloud | A bird that nests in trees | A kind of beetle | *A crew member who aims and releases bombs
exercise: «The bombardier beetle fires a boiling spray with a pop.» What is a bombardier here? | *A beetle that sprays hot chemicals | A kind of bird | A bomb-making machine
exercise: In «The bombardier beetle sprays a hot, stinging chemical», which word is the clue that tells you bombardier is an animal? | chemical | *beetle | sprays | hot
test: «The bombardier aimed at the target before the plane turned for home.» What does bombardier mean here? | A large cloud | A kind of beetle | *A crew member who aims and releases bombs | A pilot who flies the plane
test: «In the Japanese study, the bombardier beetles walked away unharmed.» Which word tells you bombardier means an animal here? | *beetles | unharmed | Japanese | study
exam: Which way is best to work out which meaning of bombardier fits a sentence? | *Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one makes sense | Look only at the word before it | Stop reading and skip the whole sentence | Guess the first meaning you ever learned
